From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 02:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: free the data of a removed affiliated AP at the
 expiry

Depends on 603-ap-mld-remove-an-affiliated-ap-at-the-expiry.patch.

At the expiry, hostapd_link_remove_finish() took the BSS out of the AP
MLD and left its station entries and its BSS data to the ucode
bss_link_removed hook, which deletes the BSS. Every other path that
takes a BSS out of the AP MLD frees its data right after
hostapd_bss_link_deinit(), and upstream frees the whole interface at
the expiry. Where the BSS outlives the hook (no ucode hook, or a hook
that keeps it), it holds references to the objects that the links of
the AP MLD share: the IEEE 802.1X authenticator, the auth_serv objects
and the RADIUS client of the first BSS. Whether a BSS frees or only
drops these depends on hostapd_mld_is_first_bss(), which returns true
for every BSS once no link is left. When the other links leave first,
the removed BSS frees them a second time:

  FREE[...]: invalid magic in os_free() <- eapol_auth_deinit()
  <- ieee802_1x_deinit() <- hostapd_deinit_wpa()
  <- hostapd_free_hapd_data()

The station entry of a non-AP MLD whose association link was removed
also stayed, with a pointer to the wpa_sm that the partner link STAs
share. clear_wpa_sm_for_all_sta() walks only the links of the AP MLD,
so a new association of the station on another link left a stale
pointer, and hostapd crashed in wpa_auth_sta_set_vlan().

Free the stations while the BSS is still a link of the AP MLD, take it
out, and then free its data, so that it releases the shared objects as
a non-first BSS and wpa_deinit() gives the primary authenticator role
to a remaining link. The hostapd_data stays allocated and stopped for
the hook or a later removal. No driver flush: the link STOP_AP already
removed the stations of the link.

Remove the link from the driver at the expiry as well.
hostapd_free_hapd_data() does that only for a BSS that is not bss[0] of
its interface; for bss[0], use link_remove_keep_bss(), as the ucode BSS
stop does. Then clear drv_priv. Before, the removal of the link waited
for a deletion of the BSS. A deletion of a stopped bss[0] (the hook,
where the radio has another BSS) no longer reached the driver: the
kernel kept the link, and the nl80211 BSS kept the freed BSS as its
context. The link removal moves that context to a remaining link. With
drv_priv cleared, the flush of a later deletion does not reach the
netdev: nl80211 sends a flush for a link that is gone without the link
ID, which removes the stations of every link.

hostapd_set_freq() and hostapd_start_dfs_cac() did not test drv_priv,
unlike the driver wrappers around them. The ucode start of an enabled
interface calls hostapd_set_freq() for each BSS, and the interference
handler and the background radar CAC use bss[0], which can be the
removed BSS: the driver then took a NULL context. Both now return as
the other wrappers do.

The ucode object of the BSS is freed with its data, before the hook,
and hostapd.uc takes the BSS from the hook's argument. The hook makes a
new object for the stopped BSS; where the hook removes the whole
interface, hostapd_interface_free() now drops the registry entry of
each BSS without an event, as hostapd_ucode_free_iface() does for the
interface.

The stopped BSS must not stay bss[0] of its interface: bss[0] holds the
driver handle and the enabled state of the interface. With drv_priv
cleared there, a BSS added to the interface took no driver handle and
crashed in wpa_driver_nl80211_if_add(), and DISABLE answered "already
disabled" while another BSS of the interface ran. Where the interface
has another BSS, move the stopped BSS behind the others and make the
next BSS the first, as the ucode BSS deletion does. Where it was the
only BSS, set the interface state to DISABLED, as upstream does at the
expiry (hostapd_disable_iface()).

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -752,6 +752,39 @@ void hostapd_mld_beacons_update(struct h
 }
 
 
+/* bss[0] holds the driver handle of the interface and its enabled state. */
+static void hostapd_link_remove_first_bss(struct hostapd_data *hapd)
+{
+	struct hostapd_iface *iface = hapd->iface;
+	struct hostapd_config *iconf = iface->conf;
+	size_t i;
+
+	if (hapd != iface->bss[0])
+		return;
+
+	/* As upstream, which disables the interface of a removed link */
+	if (iface->num_bss == 1) {
+		hostapd_set_state(iface, HAPD_IFACE_DISABLED);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	for (i = 1; i < iface->num_bss; i++)
+		iface->bss[i - 1] = iface->bss[i];
+	iface->bss[iface->num_bss - 1] = hapd;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < iconf->num_bss && iconf->bss[i] != hapd->conf; i++)
+		;
+	for (i++; i < iconf->num_bss; i++) {
+		iconf->bss[i - 1] = iconf->bss[i];
+		iconf->bss[i] = hapd->conf;
+	}
+
+	iface->bss[0]->interface_added = 0;
+	hapd->interface_added = 1;
+	hostapd_drv_set_first_bss(iface->bss[0]);
+}
+
+
 static void hostapd_link_remove_finish(void *eloop_data, void *user_ctx)
 {
 	struct hostapd_data *hapd = eloop_data;
@@ -767,7 +800,18 @@ static void hostapd_link_remove_finish(v
 	wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "MLD: Removal timer expired, link_id=%u stopped",
 		   hapd->mld_link_id);
 
+	/* Free the BSS data after it left the AP MLD, so that it releases the
+	 * objects that the links share as a non-first BSS */
+	hostapd_free_stas(hapd);
 	hostapd_bss_link_deinit(hapd);
+	/* hostapd_free_hapd_data() removes the driver link of a later BSS only */
+	if (hapd == hapd->iface->bss[0])
+		hostapd_drv_link_remove_keep_bss(hapd);
+	hostapd_free_hapd_data(hapd);
+	/* The netdev stays with the other links: a later flush without the
+	 * link would remove their stations */
+	hapd->drv_priv = NULL;
+	hostapd_link_remove_first_bss(hapd);
 	hostapd_mld_beacons_update(hapd);
 
 	hostapd_ucode_bss_cb(hapd, "bss_link_removed");
@@ -4272,6 +4316,8 @@ void hostapd_interface_free(struct hosta
 		if (iface->bss[j])
 			hostapd_mld_ref_dec(iface->bss[j]);
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
+		if (iface->bss[j])
+			hostapd_ucode_forget_bss(iface->bss[j]);
 		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "%s: free hapd %p",
 			   __func__, iface->bss[j]);
 		os_free(iface->bss[j]);
--- a/src/ap/ap_drv_ops.c
+++ b/src/ap/ap_drv_ops.c
@@ -703,7 +703,7 @@ int hostapd_set_freq(struct hostapd_data
 				    NULL, hostapd_get_punct_bitmap(hapd)))
 		return -1;
 
-	if (hapd->driver == NULL)
+	if (hapd->driver == NULL || hapd->drv_priv == NULL)
 		return 0;
 	if (hapd->driver->set_freq == NULL)
 		return 0;
@@ -1129,7 +1129,8 @@ int hostapd_start_dfs_cac(struct hostapd
 	int res;
 	struct hostapd_hw_modes *cmode = iface->current_mode;
 
-	if (!hapd->driver || !hapd->driver->start_dfs_cac || !cmode)
+	if (!hapd->driver || !hapd->driver->start_dfs_cac || !hapd->drv_priv ||
+	    !cmode)
 		return 0;
 
 	if (!iface->conf->ieee80211h) {
